Quick thought on the "how does HDP complement behavioral detection" question. Honestly, I don't think they need to complement each other in the integration sense. They each solve a different problem with a different mechanism, and the value of having both isn't that they reinforce each other technically, it's that they live in the same system and an attacker has to defeat all of them independently. Combination lock model. Identity verification, behavioral analysis, and semantic review are three separate wheels and the vault opens when all three line up. None of them is the foundation, none of them is the supplement, they each just do their job.

